WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.048
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.348 --> 00:00:08.874
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.174 --> 00:00:15.484
Unit twelve: Complexity Theory. Today you will explain emergence using result-of-interaction language.

4
00:00:15.784 --> 00:00:18.215
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:22.400
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.495
Complex system.

7
00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:31.326
Complex system means a system of many interacting parts whose behaviour cannot be predicted from the parts alone.

8
00:00:31.917 --> 00:00:35.878
An ecosystem is a complex system with countless interactions.

9
00:00:36.483 --> 00:00:39.600
Your turn. Say: Complex system.

10
00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:43.909
Complex system.

11
00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:45.802
Emergence.

12
00:00:46.817 --> 00:00:51.370
Emergence means the appearance of new properties from the interaction of simple parts.

13
00:00:51.983 --> 00:00:55.318
Consciousness may be an example of emergence.

14
00:00:55.917 --> 00:00:58.894
Your turn. Say: Emergence.

15
00:01:01.733 --> 00:01:02.874
Emergence.

16
00:01:03.617 --> 00:01:04.769
Nonlinearity.

17
00:01:05.783 --> 00:01:10.952
Nonlinearity means a relationship where small changes can cause disproportionate effects.

18
00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:15.337
Nonlinearity explains why a small rumour can crash a bank.

19
00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.893
Your turn. Say: Nonlinearity.

20
00:01:21.733 --> 00:01:23.083
Nonlinearity.

21
00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:25.085
Feedback loop.

22
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:30.335
Feedback loop means a process in which results influence the process itself.

23
00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:34.587
A reinforcing feedback loop accelerated the housing bubble.

24
00:01:35.183 --> 00:01:38.300
Your turn. Say: Feedback loop.

25
00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.179
Feedback loop.

26
00:01:42.917 --> 00:01:44.336
Self-organization.

27
00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:50.867
Self-organization means order arising spontaneously without central control.

28
00:01:51.483 --> 00:01:53.831
Flocks of birds show self-organization.

29
00:01:54.417 --> 00:01:57.406
Your turn. Say: Self-organization.

30
00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:01.662
Self-organization.

31
00:02:02.417 --> 00:02:03.360
Chaos.

32
00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:08.544
Chaos means apparent randomness that arises from deterministic rules.

33
00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.753
Weather forecasting is limited by chaos.

34
00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:15.084
Your turn. Say: Chaos.

35
00:02:17.933 --> 00:02:19.155
Chaos.

36
00:02:19.917 --> 00:02:21.312
Adaptive system.

37
00:02:22.317 --> 00:02:27.219
Adaptive system means a system that changes its behaviour in response to its environment.

38
00:02:27.817 --> 00:02:30.199
The immune system is an adaptive system.

39
00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.749
Your turn. Say: Adaptive system.

40
00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:38.054
Adaptive system.

41
00:02:38.817 --> 00:02:40.120
Interdependence.

42
00:02:41.117 --> 00:02:44.811
Interdependence means mutual reliance between parts or groups.

43
00:02:45.417 --> 00:02:48.531
Global trade has deepened economic interdependence.

44
00:02:49.117 --> 00:02:51.804
Your turn. Say: Interdependence.

45
00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:56.121
Interdependence.

46
00:02:56.933 --> 00:03:01.130
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:03:01.983 --> 00:03:07.027
Visal, ants are tiny, yet an ant colony behaves intelligently. How is that possible?

48
00:03:08.117 --> 00:03:15.285
No ant directs the colony. Intelligence emerges from the interaction of thousands of simple rules.

49
00:03:16.383 --> 00:03:18.464
So the whole is more than its parts?

50
00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:28.449
In a sense. Emergence arises from the interaction of many parts, and the pattern cannot be found in any single ant.

51
00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:31.782
Does that apply to cities or economies?

52
00:03:32.883 --> 00:03:43.268
Absolutely. Market behaviour results from countless decisions, and its feedback loops can produce stability or sudden collapse.

53
00:03:44.433 --> 00:03:46.189
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:50.489
Grammar focus: Result of interaction language.

55
00:03:50.789 --> 00:03:51.930
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:52.617 --> 00:03:55.963
Emergence arises from the interaction of many parts.

57
00:03:56.850 --> 00:04:00.765
Market behaviour results from countless individual decisions.

58
00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:04.718
Order stems from local rules, not central control.

59
00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:13.706
Use 'arise from', 'result from', 'stem from' and 'emerge from' to link an outcome to its sources. Note the preposition: from (never 'of' or 'by').

60
00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:19.506
Be careful! Don't say: Emergence arises of the interaction of parts.

61
00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:25.335
Say: Emergence arises from the interaction of parts.

62
00:04:25.635 --> 00:04:26.996
arise from (not 'of').

63
00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.092
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:32.122
More Than the Sum.

65
00:04:32.422 --> 00:04:39.286
A complex system is made of many interacting components whose collective behaviour cannot be deduced from the components alone.

66
00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:48.000
An ant colony, a rainforest and a stock market all display emergence, a pattern that arises from the interaction of countless simple parts.

67
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:57.176
Such systems are shaped by feedback loops: reinforcing loops amplify change, whereas balancing loops restore stability.

68
00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:05.704
Nonlinearity means that small causes may produce disproportionate effects, which is why long-term prediction is so difficult.

69
00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:12.055
Complexity theory therefore encourages modest forecasting and careful attention to interdependence.

70
00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:17.087
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:21.018
Emergence arises blank the interaction of parts.

72
00:05:21.318 --> 00:05:24.205
A, of. B, from. C, by.

73
00:05:27.767 --> 00:05:29.418
The answer is B: from.

74
00:05:30.583 --> 00:05:33.442
Order that appears without central control is blank.

75
00:05:33.742 --> 00:05:38.080
A, self-organization. B, chaos. C, interdependence.

76
00:05:41.633 --> 00:05:44.457
The answer is A: self-organization.

77
00:05:45.617 --> 00:05:48.661
A process whose results influence the process is a blank.

78
00:05:48.961 --> 00:05:53.555
A, feedback loop. B, substance. C, paradigm.

79
00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.204
The answer is A: feedback loop.

80
00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:01.618
Which is correct?

81
00:06:01.918 --> 00:06:09.089
A, Order results of local rules.. B, Order results from local rules.. C, Order results by of local rules..

82
00:06:12.633 --> 00:06:16.014
The answer is B: Order results from local rules..

83
00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:19.614
According to the reading, balancing loops…

84
00:06:19.914 --> 00:06:24.833
A, amplify change. B, restore stability. C, cause chaos.

85
00:06:28.367 --> 00:06:31.330
The answer is B: restore stability.

86
00:06:32.533 --> 00:06:35.697
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:40.721
Can you think of a real-world example of an emergent, complex system?

88
00:06:57.517 --> 00:06:58.924
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:59.224 --> 00:07:26.358
A traffic jam is a good example. No driver intends it, yet it emerges from the interaction of many small decisions: braking, following distance, merging. A single slowdown can spread backwards as a wave through the whole road. The pattern cannot be understood by studying one car. It arises from the system as a whole, which is the essence of emergence.

90
00:07:26.658 --> 00:07:28.437
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:33.813
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and result of interaction language.

92
00:07:34.113 --> 00:07:38.542
Today's value is systems thinking. See how the parts connect to make the whole.

93
00:07:38.842 --> 00:07:41.553
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

94
00:07:41.853 --> 00:07:44.992
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

